Keeps src/content/ in the snapshot so the directory EXISTS when `astro dev`
starts.

Astro 4 attaches its content pipeline only when the directory is already there
(node_modules/astro/dist/content/server-listeners.js: `if
(fs.existsSync(contentPaths.contentDir))`); otherwise it depends on a later
chokidar `addDir` event for the mkdir that contentOps does at edit time. When
that event was missed (2026-08-12) the collection stayed invisible for the whole
session: /__sq_post_view/{col}/{slug} rendered `No entry {col}/{slug}`.

Deliberately no config.ts: Astro 4 legacy collections are discovered by folder,
and a config that does not declare a user's collection would make getCollection
return [] for it.
